SOAPBOX: This is a challenging contest running LP unassisted into a HexBeam for the high bands and what amounts to a dummy load for the low bands but still loads of fun. I missed 4 hours during prime operating time due to family visiting (Darn family)! I generally run assisted but knew time would not allow a decent effort so I chose unassisted Classic overlay. I found it is more fun with the spots so you don’t have to search for mults. This felt like the 1990’s! Overall very pleased with the effort.
SOAPBOX: As always, I’m proud to be a part of such a kind and respectful contest community. Not only great ops, but decent people. I always finish a contest feeling much more positive about mankind.
SOAPBOX: Thanks for the contacts and look forward to many more!
SOAPBOX: 73, Jerry, AB5SE
